+++
title = "OneDrive Source"
template = "docs"
+++

The OneDrive plugin lets you **sync photos from a shared OneDrive folder** directly into your Revela project. Share a folder on OneDrive, paste the link, and your photos are downloaded automatically.

<h2 class="visually-hidden">Overview</h2>

<div class="features-grid">

### ☁️ Cloud Sync

Download photos from any OneDrive shared folder link.

### 📂 Folder Structure

Preserves the original folder hierarchy as galleries.

### ⚡ Smart Sync

Only downloads new or changed files – skips what's already there.

</div>

## Installation

The **Standalone** edition has the OneDrive plugin built in. In the **Full** edition, install it from the bundled packages:

```bash
revela plugin install Source.OneDrive
```

## Setup

```bash
# Interactive setup (recommended)
revela config onedrive

# In scripts and CI, pass the link as an option
revela config onedrive --share-url https://1drv.ms/f/your-shared-folder-link
```

`config onedrive` writes `project.json`, so run it inside your project. Without a terminal and without `--share-url` it doesn't prompt; it shows the option to pass and exits with `1`. The link must be an `https` address on `1drv.ms` or `onedrive.live.com`.

Or add the share URL directly to `project.json` below `plugins.oneDrive`:

```json
{
  "plugins": {
    "oneDrive": {
      "shareUrl": "https://1drv.ms/f/your-shared-folder-link"
    }
  }
}
```

## Usage

### Sync Photos

```bash
# Download new and changed files
revela source onedrive sync

# Preview what would be downloaded (no changes)
revela source onedrive sync --dry-run

# Force re-download all files
revela source onedrive sync --force

# Remove local files that are no longer in OneDrive (asks first)
revela source onedrive sync --clean

# Same without asking, e.g. in scripts and CI (-y)
revela source onedrive sync --clean --yes

# Remove all local files that are not in OneDrive, ignoring include/exclude patterns
revela source onedrive sync --clean-all

# List every affected file (combine with --dry-run to preview)
revela source onedrive sync --dry-run --show-files

# Use a different share link for this run only
revela source onedrive sync --share-url https://1drv.ms/f/another-link
```

The short aliases are `-n` (`--dry-run`), `-f` (`--force`), `-u` (`--share-url`) and `-y` (`--yes`).

> **Careful with `--clean`:** local images and Markdown files that aren't in the OneDrive folder count as orphans. If your `source` folder also has photos or pages that don't come from OneDrive, preview with `--dry-run --show-files` first. Outside a terminal (scripts, CI) Revela cannot ask, so `--clean` stops before downloading or deleting anything unless you add `--yes`.

### Full Workflow

```bash
# 1. Configure share link
revela config onedrive

# 2. Sync photos
revela source onedrive sync

# 3. Generate site
revela generate all
```

In the Full edition, run `revela plugin install Source.OneDrive` first. You can also connect OneDrive while creating a project: the project wizard offers it as an optional step.

## Configuration

```json
{
  "plugins": {
    "oneDrive": {
      "shareUrl": "https://1drv.ms/f/your-link",
      "defaultConcurrency": 4,
      "includePatterns": ["*.jpg", "*.jpeg", "*.png", "*.tiff", "*.md", "_index.revela"],
      "excludePatterns": ["*.tmp"]
    }
  }
}
```

| Option | Required | Default | Description |
|--------|----------|---------|-------------|
| `shareUrl` | Yes | – | OneDrive shared folder URL |
| `defaultConcurrency` | No | `4` | Parallel downloads (increase for fast connections) |
| `includePatterns` | No | All files | File-name patterns to download (`*`, `?`, case-insensitive) |
| `excludePatterns` | No | None | File-name patterns to skip; exclusion wins over inclusion |

Patterns match the file name only, not the folder path. Without `includePatterns`,
`--clean` only considers local images (`.jpg`, `.jpeg`, `.png`, `.webp`) and
Markdown files; excluded files are never downloaded or cleaned up.

## Supported Link Formats

- `https://1drv.ms/f/...` – short links
- `https://onedrive.live.com/...` – full links

Both public and organization-shared folders are supported.

## Progress Display

The plugin shows a two-phase progress display:

1. **Scanning** – discovers files and folders with a spinner
2. **Downloading** – progress bar with file count and remaining time

```
⠋ Scanning OneDrive folder...
✓ Found 142 files in 8 folders

Downloading (42/142) vacation/sunset.jpg  ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━  29%  ETA 02:15
```

When the output is not a terminal (CI logs, `> sync.log`), the spinner and progress bar are replaced by plain lines, one about every 10 %.

## Environment Variables

All settings can be overridden with environment variables:

```bash
SPECTARA__REVELA__PLUGINS__ONEDRIVE__SHAREURL=https://1drv.ms/f/...
SPECTARA__REVELA__PLUGINS__ONEDRIVE__DEFAULTCONCURRENCY=8
```

## Requirements

- OneDrive shared folder link (public or organization-shared)
- Internet connection for syncing
- Files up to 1 GB each; a larger file stops the sync with an error and keeps any existing local copy
